<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lecha Dodi</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">16th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">liturgical song taking many passages from it, its opening two words among them</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Canticum Canticorum (Giovanni Pierluigi da Palestrina)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1584</span><span class="sg-chain-h">29 five-part motets setting the text</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chi è costei (Francesca Caccini)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1618</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting of 6:10</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphoniae sacrae I (Heinrich Schütz)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1629</span><span class="sg-chain-h">settings of the text</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Membra Jesu Nostri: Vulnerasti cor meum (Dieterich Buxtehude)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1680</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cantata setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wachet auf, ruft uns die Stimme (J. S. Bach, BWV 140)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cantata using its words and imagery</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Flos Campi (Ralph Vaughan Williams)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1925</span><span class="sg-chain-h">suite, each movement headed by a verse</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Le Cantique des Cantiques (Jean-Yves Daniel-Lesur)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1952</span><span class="sg-chain-h">choral setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Song of Songs (Marc Chagall)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1957–1966</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cycle of five paintings</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Little Foxes (Lillian Hellman)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1939</span><span class="sg-chain-h">play titled from 2:15</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Grapes of Wrath (John Steinbeck)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1939</span><span class="sg-chain-h">character named Rose of Sharon, an epithet of the Song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Das Hohelied Salomos (Popol Vuh)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">album named after it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Song of Solomon (Toni Morrison)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">novel titled after it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Asma Asmaton (Vangelis and Irene Papas)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1986</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Song of Solomon (Kate Bush)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1993</span><span class="sg-chain-h">song quoting it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Shir Ha-Shirim (John Zorn)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">work for five female singers and narrators</span></li></ul></section>
